Description: USB library import of rekordbox/Serato drives (DECKSMITHOS_USB_IMPORT)
 With DECKSMITHOS_USB_IMPORT set to colon separated mount points ("/usb:/usb2";
 labels USB, USB2, ...), Mixxx polls every 2 s whether a file system other
 than "/" is mounted there. When a drive appears, a library rescan is
 requested and, in a worker thread, the rekordbox export (export.pdb) and the
 Serato crates (_Serato_/Subcrates/*.crate, order from neworder.pref) are
 read. After the scan, rekordbox playlists and Serato crates become locked
 Mixxx playlists named "USB ▸ Folder ▸ Playlist" in rekordbox/Serato order and
 track order, listed first in the Playlists section (table
 decksmithos_usb_playlists holds their sort order). The rekordbox analysis
 (beat grid, hot cues, memory cues, loops, phrases) plus key and color is
 read in the background and applied to the library tracks in small batches in
 the GUI thread; rekordbox always wins, unchanged tracks are not touched. A
 drive track loaded into a player before that gets its data right before
 loading. Playlists of a drive are deleted when it is removed, when it
 appears and at startup. Nothing is written to the drive.
 The ANLZ/PDB reading of RekordboxFeature moved to rekordboxanalysis.cpp
 (shared; cue lists are no longer imported twice from PCOB and PCO2, hot
 loops keep their length, uncolored memory cues get the default color,
 malformed files are logged instead of crashing) and Serato crate parsing to
 seratocrate.cpp.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
